      "side": 1,
      "message": "The style guide prohibits the use of the `NULL` macro or the `0` integer literal for pointers.\n\nIn **`crypto_util.cc`**, the OpenSSL API calls use `NULL`:\n\n```c\nif (EVP_EncryptInit_ex(ctx.get(), EVP_aes_256_gcm(), NULL, NULL, NULL) !\u003d 1 ||\n    EVP_CIPHER_CTX_ctrl(ctx.get(), EVP_CTRL_GCM_SET_IVLEN, iv.size(), NULL) !\u003d 1 ||\n    EVP_EncryptInit_ex(ctx.get(), NULL, NULL, key.data(), iv.data()) !\u003d 1) {\n\n```\n\n**Fix:** Replace all instances of `NULL` passed to `EVP_*` functions with `nullptr`. OpenSSL C APIs safely accept `nullptr` in modern C++ environments.",
